            <ArticleTitle>Use of SafeCut Balloon for treatment of in-stent restenosis of a previously underexpanded sirolimus-eluting stent with a heavily calcified plaque.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E359-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Calcified lesions are a cause of stent underexpansion which significantly increases the subsequent risks of in-stent restenosis and thrombosis, even when drug-eluting stents are used. In this report, we describe a novel balloon catheter (SafeCut) that enabled adequate dilatation of in-stent restenosis in a previously underexpanded sirolimus-eluting stent that was unresponsive to high-pressure inflation using a conventional balloon after aggressive rotational atherectomy to treat a heavily calcified plaque.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
